.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Dirichlet proved in 1837 that every progression a, a+q, a+2q, \dots with \gcd(a, q) = 1 contains infinitely many primes, and the classes share the primes equally in the limit. Equal in the limit is not equal at every point: the race between primes \equiv 3 and \equiv 1 \pmod 4 is led by the 3s almost all the time (&quot;Chebyshev&#x27;s bias&quot;, 1853).">

